From b05a1202138ad50efbb859087a4d87d0067ddd6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Software Engineer <software-engineer@dcxxiv.local>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:47:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: ship resolved kernel config as package content, name
 build mode (DCX-99)

scripts/verify-resolved-i2c-off.sh asserted CONFIG_I2C against
configs/kernel.config on the premise that the kernel ebuild's src_install
had overwritten it with the resolved post-olddefconfig config. That never
happens on a binpkg cache hit, so the assertion silently checked the
pinned config and always passed vacuously.

Ship the resolved .config as gzipped package content instead
(/usr/share/monolith-kernel/resolved-kernel.config.gz, monolith-kernel
r7 -> r8 to bust the stale binpkg). That file rides inside the binpkg's
CONTENTS, so it is populated identically on a source build or a cache
hit -- no source/binary branching needed, and a missing artifact is a
loud FAIL instead of a silent pass-through to a stale file. Also:

- stops silently swallowing a failed copy-back of the /configs
  dev-convenience copy (cp ... || true -> || die)
- excludes the proof artifact from the shipped rootfs (486-minimalism)
- classifies binpkg vs. source from the emerge log in build.yml and
  threads that label through to the PASS/FAIL line, so CI can no
  longer print the same-looking line in both modes (Code Reviewer
  finding #2 on the prior attempt)
- documents the agent git-env workaround (GIT_CONFIG_COUNT) and adds
  scripts/agent-git-env.sh so this fix and its handoff notes survive
  future runs (DCX-131)

Co-Authored-By: Paperclip <noreply@paperclip.ing>
